# 250-APP-0024 — The word error rate of our engine: 5.10 % in Russian, 11.96 % in English, as the published models — done

**Type:** tools (voice) · **Owner:** tools track (`APP`) · **Priority:** P2 · **Status:** done (2026-10-09) · **Blocked by:** — · **Main task:** [250](../issues/250-voice-dictation.md) (step 4, and step 8 on the host) · **Roadmap:** track G · **Constitution:** MC-12.1, MC-12.2

## Problem

Acceptance of 250: with our int8 weights, WER on the 272 Russian FLEURS sentences must be within 0.5 points of the 5.20 % measured for the published model. Until now our engine had been compared with onnxruntime on ten clips only, and with onnxruntime's features rather than ours.

The English model (Zipformer GigaSpeech, step 8) had not been converted at all. Converting it showed two problems:

- It uses three operators the interpreter lacked: `ReduceMax`, `Greater` and `Identity`.
- `convert.py` put the names of all three graphs in one table. Each graph has its own `/Constant_output_0`, and the decoder's overwrote the encoder's: an index of 1 where the encoder has -1.
  - In the English encoder this made a `Gather` read out of range.
  - In the Russian model the same thing happened, but harmlessly: the encoder's output and text are the same before and after the fix.

## Plan

- **The test `word_error_rate_of_a_test_set`** in `tests/nn_host.rs`, run by hand with `MIND_DICTATE_MODEL` and `MIND_DICTATE_SET`. It runs the whole chain:
  - reads the WAVs;
  - computes our features (`mind::voice::fbank`);
  - runs our network;
  - runs greedy search (`mind::voice::dictation`, shared with the program `dictate`).

  It normalizes text as `scripts/voice_v3/evaluate.py` does: lower case, ё as е, no punctuation. WER and CER are counted over the whole set, as jiwer counts them.
- **`convert.py`:** each top graph has its own names, which its `If` branches share.
- **`mind::nn`:**
  - `ReduceMax`, `Greater` and `Identity`;
  - an operator's error names the node's first output, so a failure points at its node.

## Acceptance criteria

- The Russian model's WER on the 272 sentences is within 0.5 points of 5.20 %.
- The English model runs, and its WER on the 281 English sentences is reported beside the published int8 model's 11.98 %.
- The new operators are tested against values worked out by hand (`tests/nn_host.rs`, in CI).

## Resolution

- **Measured on this host** (one thread, AVX2, our features), on the sets of [scripts/voice_v3](../scripts/voice_v3/README.md):

  | Model | Sentences | WER % | CER % | Published model (sherpa-onnx), WER / CER % | Time |
  |---|---|---|---|---|---|
  | `vosk-model-ru` 0.54 | 272, 51 min | **5.10** (265 of 5196 words) | 1.28 | 5.20 / 1.30 | 0.099 of real time |
  | Zipformer GigaSpeech, int8 | 281, 45 min | **11.96** (736 of 6154 words) | 7.28 | 11.98 / 7.34 | 0.095 of real time |

  Our engine is as accurate as onnxruntime's on these sets. The small differences are int8 quantization noise ([250-APP-0021](250-APP-0021-network-interpreter.done)).

  The times were measured with other jobs running on the host, and they are the host's (MC-12.1).
- **Code:**
  - [`tests/nn_host.rs`](../tests/nn_host.rs);
  - [`libmind/src/voice/dictation.rs`](../libmind/src/voice/dictation.rs): greedy search, moved out of the test;
  - [`libmind/src/nn/ops.rs`](../libmind/src/nn/ops.rs) and [`mod.rs`](../libmind/src/nn/mod.rs);
  - [`scripts/voice_dictate/convert.py`](../scripts/voice_dictate/convert.py).
- **Files made before this fix must be converted again.**

